-- title:
--   Theorem 17 host: the residue classes and the chunks, followed by any statement (classes_then)
-- statement:
--   A sequencing lemma for the host program of Theorem 17 (the reduction of Exact Triangle to Lop-AE-SparseTri), about the two calls that sort the pairs by residue class and cut the classes into chunks.
--
--   Let $P$ be a program of the light language whose procedures $p_{\mathrm{classes}}$ and $p_{\mathrm{chunks}}$ are the bodies of `classes` and `chunks`. Let $x$ be an Exact Triangle instance with $n$ vertices per part and weight bound $U$, and $X$ the data of the host's run (the prime $p$, the capacity $\mathit{cap}\ge1$ of a chunk, the residues of the weights), and assume the host is *ready* at depth $d$ in memory $\mu$ with free pointer $f$: the three $n\times n$ weight matrices are stored below $f$ with entries of absolute value at most $U$, $1\le p$, $p\cdot2^{\mathrm{bitLen}(U)+1}$ and every address fit in a word, the arrays of the host fit in memory and $d+2\le\mathrm{depth}$. Let $\mu_1$ be a memory holding the residues $r_{AB}$ of the first matrix modulo $p$ at their array.
--
--   Suppose a statement $t$ satisfies: for every result $r'$ and every memory $\mu'$ that holds the pairs sorted class by class and the table of chunks (their residues, starts and lengths) and agrees with $\mu_1$ outside the area between the class array and the first instance matrix, $t$ run from the host's local frame (with the number of chunks set) ends within $T-(t_{\mathrm{classes}}(n,p)+t_{\mathrm{chunks}}(p,k)+17)$ steps with postcondition $Q$, where $k$ is the number of chunks. If moreover $t_{\mathrm{classes}}(n,p)+t_{\mathrm{chunks}}(p,k)+17\le T$, then the sequence
--   $$\mathtt{Small} := p_{\mathrm{classes}}(\dots);\quad \mathtt{NumChunks} := p_{\mathrm{chunks}}(\dots);\quad t$$
--   run from the host's local frame in memory $\mu_1$ ends within $T$ steps with postcondition $Q$.
--
--   The lemma lets the proofs of the host compose the classes-and-chunks phase with whatever follows it, here the loop over the instances of the all-edges host at the middle dimension.
--
--   **Formalization Note** This is the lemma `Light.Sec3.Et17.classes_then` of the unmodified library; it is a platform node because the all-edges host at the middle dimension reuses it. The local variable names (`ResAB`, `Size`, `ThePrime`, `Cls`, …) are the slots of the host's frame `Et17.locals`.
-- source:
--   Lean formalization anthropics/formal-math, folder 3sum-apsp, commit e1a4e65, file https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/blob/e1a4e6508154ea59f030480661590a9fe3018011/3sum-apsp/ThreeSumApsp/Programs/Sec3/Theorem17/Host/Arrays.lean#L182-L194 (unmodified lemma of the library; its definitions are taken from the platform bundles APSP299791_Defs1 to APSP299791_Defs5). Proof of Theorem 17 (p. 33) of J. Alman and V. Vassilevska Williams, "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in Sparse Lopsided Graphs", arXiv:2610.06783v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783v1).

